<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="sec-structure">
  <title>Subsets</title>
  <definition xml:id="def-subset">
    <p>
      A set <m>A</m> is a <term>subset</term> of <m>B</m> when every element of <m>A</m> is also an element of <m>B</m>.
    </p>
  </definition>
  <p>The subset relation has two basic properties.</p>
  <ol>
    <p>Reflexive: <m>A \subseteq A</m>.</p>
    <li><p>Transitive: if <m>A \subseteq B</m> and <m>B \subseteq C</m> then <m>A \subseteq C</m>.</p></li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    By <xref ref="thm-partial-order"/>, the subset relation is a partial order.
  </p>
  <p>
    The diagram below illustrates the relation.
    <figure xml:id="fig-venn">
      <caption>A subset drawn inside its superset.</caption>
      <image source="images/venn-subset.png"/>
    </figure>
  </p>
</section>
